# T3CHNRD Digital Field Kit
# Keep source in Git; exclude field data, generated output, caches, large third-party payloads, and secrets.

# --- Diagnostic/runtime output ---
Diagnostic-Reports/
**/Diagnostic-Reports/
Reports/
**/Reports/
Logs/
**/Logs/
*.log
*.etl
*.evtx
*.dmp
*.mdmp
*.dump
*.trace
*.tmp
*.temp
*.pid
*.lock

# --- Runtime/broker state ---
*.runner.txt
*.runner.log
*.done
*.ready
*.cancel
*.heartbeat
*.request
broker.error
broker.ready
heartbeat.txt
shutdown.txt

# --- Runbook field/company content ---
# The Runbook engine/templates belong in Git; technician/company documents do not.
Runbook/
runbook project/
**/Runbook/Attachments/
**/Runbook/Imported/

# --- Local AI payloads ---
*.gguf
*.ggml
*.safetensors
AI/models/
ai/models/
AI/runtime/
ai/runtime/

# --- Python ---
.venv/
.venv*/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Node / Electron future shell ---
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.electron/
dist/
out/
release/

# --- .NET / build output ---
bin/
obj/
[Bb]uild/
[Bb]uilds/
*.user
*.suo
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.cache

# --- Installer/build artifacts ---
Installer/Output/
**/Installer/Output/
*.msi
*.msix
*.appx
*.appxbundle
*.dmg
*.pkg

# --- Third-party redistributables / large binary setup payloads ---
# Keep manifests, download/build instructions, licenses, and checksums in Git instead.
R/Setup/Apps/*.exe
R/Setup/Apps/*.msi
R/Setup/WinUtil/**/bin/
ThirdParty/Binaries/
third_party/binaries/

# --- Secrets / local configuration ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
secrets/
Secrets/
local.settings.json

# --- Editor / OS clutter ---
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- Archives generated for field testing ---
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar

# Keep repository documentation and source manifests tracked.
!docs/
!Docs/
!**/*.md
!**/*.txt
